        <!-- FAQ -->
        <div id="faq" class="scroll-mt-24 mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            12. Frequently Asked Questions
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is the best car battery?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                There is no single best car battery for every vehicle. For most modern cars, especially those with start-stop, a mainstream AGM such as the DieHard Platinum AGM, Duracell Ultra Platinum AGM or Interstate MTX in the correct group size is the right choice. For trucks and cold climates, the Odyssey Extreme Series is the premium pick, and for older cars without start-stop, a fresh flooded battery like the EverStart Maxx is the value buy.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Is an AGM car battery worth it?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                An AGM car battery is worth it, and often required, if your car has start-stop, came with AGM from the factory, carries heavy electronic loads, sits for long periods or sees a lot of vibration. For an older car with a simple electrical system that came with a flooded battery, AGM is optional. A fresh flooded battery usually delivers better value there, though AGM's longer life can partly offset the higher price.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">How long does a car battery last?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Most car batteries last about three to five years, but climate makes a big difference. Heat speeds up internal corrosion and water loss, so batteries in hot regions often fail sooner, and the damage usually shows up the following winter. Short trips, long parking without a maintainer and a weak charging system also shorten life. Test the battery yearly once it passes three years old.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Are Duracell car batteries good?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Duracell auto battery reviews are generally in line with other mainstream brands, because Duracell licenses its name to an established automotive battery manufacturer. The Ultra Platinum AGM is a conventional flat-plate AGM suited to start-stop and electronics-heavy vehicles. Buy it for price and availability at warehouse clubs, check the date code, and keep the receipt for any warranty claim.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">How do I read a car battery date code?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                There is no single standard. Many batteries now carry a sticker showing month and year. Others use a code where a letter stands for the month, starting with A for January, and a digit stands for the year. Some makers stamp a longer manufacturing code into the case. If you cannot decode it, ask the store or check the maker's website, which usually explains its format.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Can a portable power station jump-start a car?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Generally no. A portable power station's 12V car-style port is usually limited to around 10 amps, while a starter draws hundreds of amps, so the station will shut down to protect itself. Some power stations are sold with jump-start functions, but most are not. Use a dedicated lithium jump starter or cables, or plug a battery charger into the station's AC outlet to recharge slowly.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Do I need to register a new car battery?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Many newer vehicles with battery monitoring systems, including models from BMW, Mercedes-Benz, Audi, Volkswagen, Ford and others, need a new battery registered or the battery monitor reset. That tells the charging system it has a fresh battery, and on some cars, which type and capacity it is. Skipping it can lead to overcharging or undercharging and a shorter battery life. A shop scan tool or a capable consumer scanner can do it.
              </p>
            </div>

          </div>
