          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most modern cars, the best car battery is a fresh, mainstream AGM in the exact group size your manual calls for: the DieHard Platinum AGM, Duracell Ultra Platinum AGM or Interstate MTX, chosen by where you can get warranty service. Step up to the Odyssey Extreme Series or an Optima only when cold, vibration, accessories or long storage give you a reason, and save money with the EverStart Maxx on an older car without start-stop.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you buy, check the date code, test the charging system before blaming the battery, and keep a jump starter in the car. A good battery will start your car for years; a jump starter means that the day it does not is an inconvenience rather than a tow.
